{"scraped_at": "2026-06-04T07:26:16.694941+00:00", "run_id": "20260604_072616", "page": 18, "api_response": {"count": 3946, "per_page": 20, "current_page": 18, "total_pages": 198, "next": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=19&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "previous": "https://tripadvisor-scraper-api.omkar.cloud/reviews?query=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.tripadvisor.com%2FAttraction_Review-g293890-d310712-Reviews-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html&page=17&sort_by=most_recent&locale=en-US", "results": [{"review_id": 720990867, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r720990867-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Different totally", "text": "Different culture, could not be the best to see but feel its culture what we taught and give . Life ending place to explore different ways of celebration ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "D65713B07C877F1724536AE78432B3CF", "name": "skl b", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sklb2014", "username": "sklb2014", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/f3/e4/default-avatar-2020-30.jpg", "contribution_count": 24, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 186338, "location_name": "London", "location_name_detailed": "London, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-24", "published_at_date": "2019-10-24"}, {"review_id": 720457142, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r720457142-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Facinating to see", "text": "This temple holds open cremation ceremonies for the Hindus.  It is a compelling sight.  A must see.  We did have our guide, Rabina, with us to add insight and context during our visit to this World Heritage Site.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "C3F2A9271FCB5B3832979B6BF282F280", "name": "Lisa S", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/lisas521", "username": "lisas521", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e3/1f/default-avatar-2020-46.jpg", "contribution_count": 14, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c7/2f/9c/the-deceased-loved-one.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c7/2f/fb/the-deceased-loved-one.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-10-22", "published_at_date": "2019-10-22"}, {"review_id": 720380505, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r720380505-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Moving!!", "text": "It seems strange to be able to see people grieving as their loved ones are cremated, but the celebration of life makes this a must see place. The cremations are carried out with care and love.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "4E10CA72FF3C8D44D43AAC141FC17D66", "name": "Fergus and Siobhan", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/Toonloony", "username": "Toonloony", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/e4/1a/8f/toonloony.jpg", "contribution_count": 16, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 315977, "location_name": "Market Harborough", "location_name_detailed": "Market Harborough, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-22", "published_at_date": "2019-10-22"}, {"review_id": 720283291, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r720283291-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Nepal - The Land of Worship and Wonder - A Positive Experience with Gyan Bahadur Mukhiya", "text": "After an exhausting and \" adventurous \" bus trip from Gyriong to Kathmandu and only a few hours of sleep, we were lucky to be able to do a lot of sightseeing under the wonderful guidance of Gyan Bahadur Muhkiya ( we simply called him GYAN). \nGyan was hard working, prompt, personable and very efficient. He not only guided us to visit all important places of interest, he helped us with other errands like exchanging money,  selecting a good restaurant, shopping for some particular souvenirs, items of clothing, he would gladly helped.  Some times I think he got overwhelmed as he tried to accommodate all 16 of us.  \nHe has good knowledge about history, religion and the Kathmandu area.  With such a tight schedule, he managed to take us to many wonderful \" not to miss\" places of interest.  Yes, we visited Swayambunath, Pashupatinath temple.  They are such beautiful temples with interesting religious and culture differences.  Gyan explained to us the funeral tradition in the river, the cremation and we watched the sacred ceremony with flowers and tears ….and were simply amazed. \nOf course, we visited Kathmandu City, Pagan among other places and the ladies got their shopping done too.\nGiven how crowded those places were, such a large group we were and  the limited amount of time we had, I think Gyan did a wonderful job as a nice, patient and caring tour guide.\nI certainly recommend Gyan for those of you who want to travel to Nepal.  In addition to English, Gyan speaks Japanese and French .", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 2, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-09-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "8E0067FB25F1E3AD76AE4E353E069BC5", "name": "@77059Happytraveler", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/77059Happytraveler", "username": "77059Happytraveler", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e8/5b/default-avatar-2020-61.jpg", "contribution_count": 41, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 56003, "location_name": "Houston", "location_name_detailed": "Houston, Texas"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-22", "published_at_date": "2019-10-22"}, {"review_id": 720256651, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r720256651-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Incredible experience", "text": "I sat with many others on the far bank of the Holy River, mesmerised watching the   rituals as the Hindus laid there loved ones to rest.  As the bodies are washed, the funeral pyre is prepared.  The temple and grounds cover a large area.  There are souvenir stalls and plenty of car parking.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "E23CDEE753382F675C95FA77E0E8A248", "name": "Andrew H", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/ajhaeh", "username": "ajhaeh", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c6/0b/01/andrew-h.jpg", "contribution_count": 2851, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 580426, "location_name": "Rochdale", "location_name_detailed": "Rochdale, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c4/e2/6f/pashupati-nath.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c4/e2/b0/pashupati-nath.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c4/e2/e0/pashupati-nath.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c4/e2/f7/pashupati-nath.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/c4/e3/0b/pashupati-nath.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-10-21", "published_at_date": "2019-10-21"}, {"review_id": 720200298, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r720200298-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Culturally significant", "text": "A must if you're visiting Nepal.  The Hindu funeral traditions here are important to observe (from a respectful distance) for the Western traveler.  It differs so much from most Western cultural practices.  A great way to get a look into this wonderful, beautiful land.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": null, "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "FB23DCFC1879FD8BDA7BE7DFD1876035", "name": "Christy C", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/TempuraMoon", "username": "TempuraMoon", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/21/d8/66/1d/caption.jpg", "contribution_count": 88, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 42195, "location_name": "Farmington Hills", "location_name_detailed": "Farmington Hills, Michigan"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-21", "published_at_date": "2019-10-21"}, {"review_id": 719398135, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r719398135-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Worship Shiva", "text": "We visited Pashupatinath temple in kathmandu. Such a beautiful temple .we worshiped god shiva with milk and Rudrabhishekam.. Nice pooja. We feel for just a minute i tie with shivji ji . Feeling better and feel that i was fly in the sky. Beautiful moment of my life. We got prasadam and we see all the shivlings . We drop coin in the backside river . We also see one new thing  infront me a dead body was funeral. It was vertical horirble for us .then outside the temple we bought pearls strings for relatives and come back at the hotel", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2018-11-30"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "1A26389E2680DE1C221AD6CE4D319195", "name": "sushilgarg778", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/sushilgarg778", "username": "sushilgarg778", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e2/e6/default-avatar-2020-45.jpg", "contribution_count": 77, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 304551, "location_name": "New Delhi", "location_name_detailed": "New Delhi, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-18", "published_at_date": "2019-10-18"}, {"review_id": 719301188, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r719301188-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Excellent", "text": "Excellent temple in Khatmandu, it is a must visit place , generally there are long queues to offer puja.", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "family", "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "F8553DB6F0F5BCB79526559821CA8184", "name": "KoleyA", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/KoleyA", "username": "KoleyA", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e9/ef/default-avatar-2020-66.jpg", "contribution_count": 137, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 9456047, "location_name": "Burdwan", "location_name_detailed": "Burdwan, India"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-18", "published_at_date": "2019-10-18"}, {"review_id": 719294540, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r719294540-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Temple not for foreigners but cremations open to all", "text": "We were not allowed inside the confines of the temple as it is restricted to Hindus only, which, given its religious significance is reasonable enough\nOur guide then took us to the river where corpses are washed prior to being processed to the funeral pyre where the body is placed and cremated in full public view. Close family members also have heads shaved. This is a fascinating insight into their culture but we did feel somewhat intrusive at a time of grief and mourning for the families, but our guide assured us that it is seen as respect not intrusion\nOnce the body is burned, which takes around 3 - 4 hours the stone beneath the pyre is unceremoniously scrubbed down and the remaining bones washed into the river before a new pyre is set for the next corpse\nA lesson in life and death", "review_tip": null, "rating": 4, "subratings": [], "like_count": 1, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "couples", "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "BE73E61999235CEC220CDBA7E61EC3EE", "name": "HSeeingtheworld", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/HSeeingtheworld", "username": "HSeeingtheworld", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/1a/f6/e8/5b/default-avatar-2020-61.jpg", "contribution_count": 553, "hometown": {"tripadvisor_entity_id": 2091417, "location_name": "Welwyn", "location_name_detailed": "Welwyn, United Kingdom"}, "is_verified": false}, "images": [], "created_at_date": "2019-10-18", "published_at_date": "2019-10-18"}, {"review_id": 719126335, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r719126335-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "title": "Fascinating!", "text": "I loved our visit; i should have gone ahead and hired a guide. The complex is beautiful and we were a little hesitant where we could and couldn’t go and if photos were ok. ", "review_tip": null, "rating": 5, "subratings": [], "like_count": 0, "language": "en", "is_translated": false, "original_language": "en", "owner_response": null, "trip": {"trip_type": "friends", "stay_date": "2019-10-31"}, "reviewer": {"reviewer_id": "B261EE993202F9BCFBE85EA1FE4654B8", "name": "pokemom", "profile_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/Profile/pokemom", "username": "pokemom", "avatar": "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-s/01/34/a0/3b/pokemom.jpg", "contribution_count": 398, "hometown": null, "is_verified": false}, "images": ["https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/ab/40/87/photo0jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/ab/40/88/photo1jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/ab/40/89/photo2jpg.jpg", "https://dynamic-media-cdn.tripadvisor.com/media/photo-o/19/ab/40/8a/photo3jpg.jpg"], "created_at_date": "2019-10-17", "published_at_date": "2019-10-17"}, {"review_id": 719071755, "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r719071755-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html", "